<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-09-12T04:46:08Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>France: More than 40 injured in train derailment</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5a1ba1bf4b6033abf99eb48e2455c8ca5d3151c012f6ce6c76b560ef34b9a08e</id><updated>2026-09-12T04:46:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T21:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-more-than-40-injured-in-train-derailment/a-79241365--ae760899c756.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-more-than-40-injured-in-train-derailment/a-79241365?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The train derailed between Rouen and Caen in Normandy, northwest France, on Friday evening. One of the injured was in a critical state.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Russian strike on Kyiv gas station kills 2</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:090ccb533a3ebb79e9e21db52303e8000e0033e83b837948a65d21822968412b</id><updated>2026-09-12T04:45:10Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T15:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-russian-strike-on-kyiv-gas-station-kills-2/a-79238219--1e875d361611.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-russian-strike-on-kyiv-gas-station-kills-2/a-79238219?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With fighting on the front lines mostly stalled, Russia has been increasingly hitting petrol stations and other civilian targets. Ukraine has also been attacking Russia with drones, killing three people on Friday.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US commemorates 25 years since 9/11 terror attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:16536357db94fa38c5e3a3490dd6261446562efff6166da2245b3ad9915408bd</id><updated>2026-09-12T04:45:10Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T15:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-commemorates-25-years-since-9-11-terror-attack/a-79237898--048849ac59b3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-commemorates-25-years-since-9-11-terror-attack/a-79237898?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A quarter century has passed since Islamists hijacked four commercial jets and turned them into weapons against the US. On Friday, ceremonies in New York, Pennsylvania and Washington DC marked the dark anniversary.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Iran pursues cautious escalation ahead of US midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c7b3f846409b6e4b5f3b5eefdfdb37a8b5b325625986d1f88f28c6fbbf150462</id><updated>2026-09-12T04:45:10Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T14:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-pursues-cautious-escalation-ahead-of-us-midterms/a-79237061--fcf56cfd7af3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-pursues-cautious-escalation-ahead-of-us-midterms/a-79237061?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Tehran appears to be boosting pressure on Washington ahead of the crucial midterm vote, but shows little desire to return to a full-scale war.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India's BRICS strategy tested with Xi, Putin set to visit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:24e4dbb8d74f9cf2528d1c86d8687d4ecca0483a6c981a10ba036ad47911f556</id><updated>2026-09-12T04:45:10Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T13:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-s-brics-strategy-tested-with-xi-putin-set-to-visit/a-79231879--3d59ee566cca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-s-brics-strategy-tested-with-xi-putin-set-to-visit/a-79231879?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">New Delhi's "America Plus" approach sees India deepening its ties with China and Russia, while also trying to keep BRICS from turning into an anti-Western platform.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Uber leaves two key African markets — and their drivers in despair</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0a779aaec64101c867241d1c98fd38e3e5279974ab83ade98fab3c153410006a</id><updated>2026-09-12T04:45:10Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T12:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uber-leaves-two-key-african-markets-and-their-drivers-in-despair/a-79232189--bdbc88dc3498.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uber-leaves-two-key-african-markets-and-their-drivers-in-despair/a-79232189?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Uber's departure from Nigeria and Uganda has left countless customers high and dry. But what about drivers? With fuel prices, maintenance and other operating costs rising, many say they're struggling to make a living.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>BRICS Summit 2026: Putin, Modi reaffirm partnership</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:63fbdd7e4840778d6a66b01901c07ae2db0fa41232469b61cca654063387dd91</id><updated>2026-09-12T04:45:10Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T12:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/brics-summit-2026-putin-modi-reaffirm-partnership/live-79224239--ae45dba23a6f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/brics-summit-2026-putin-modi-reaffirm-partnership/live-79224239?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Modi will also meet Xi Jinping as India seeks to balance ties with China and Russia. The wars in Ukraine and Iran could test the group's unity at the summit. Follow DW for more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Iran war: Saudi-Houthi escalation intensifies Yemen conflict</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6559b3b4fd41d3a23aff553acea0f60382eab022f22990d084c3a60a51c462d6</id><updated>2026-09-12T04:45:10Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T11:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-war-saudi-houthi-escalation-intensifies-yemen-conflict/a-79226627--c5b66c310724.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-war-saudi-houthi-escalation-intensifies-yemen-conflict/a-79226627?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Houthi takeovers of Mokha, Dhubab and Perim in the Bab el-Mandeb Strait threaten to push Yemen deeper into the Middle East war. The Iran-backed group has made advances against Yemen's government and Saudi Arabia.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany charges 7 suspected Hamas members over attack plot</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4262f2047b055ee5cfe673b8f1e4ed5538ce7880e3886a6c5c2f8f071da3b58a</id><updated>2026-09-12T04:45:10Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T11:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-charges-7-suspected-hamas-members-over-attack-plot/a-79230171--a30b5fe0228d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-charges-7-suspected-hamas-members-over-attack-plot/a-79230171?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prosecutors say the suspects had moved beyond general preparations and were already pursuing a concrete plan for a deadly attack on Israeli or Jewish targets.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>9/11 conspiracy theories that continue to circulate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7d072368185d5db49c0231844515dd6ed43ccf0f88f0bf33bde0453ace5f6df2</id><updated>2026-09-12T04:45:10Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T11:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/9-11-conspiracy-theories-that-continue-to-circulate/a-78896069--975de526f230.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/9-11-conspiracy-theories-that-continue-to-circulate/a-78896069?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A quarter-century after the September 11, 2001, attacks, they are still the focus of numerous conspiracy theories. Why do people believe them?</summary><category term="TOP STORIES" /></entry><entry><title>India looks to steer BRICS away from anti-Western turn</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:286234b624cb12fd43252b325b475cd010653ec49e719f372c57efa9dfe24018</id><updated>2026-09-12T04:45:10Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T10:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-looks-to-steer-brics-away-from-anti-western-turn/a-79195234--e9a076e9f28e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-looks-to-steer-brics-away-from-anti-western-turn/a-79195234?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The BRICS summit 2026 takes place in Delhi this weekend. Unlike last year, Putin and Xi are expected to attend. Can India keep the expanded bloc united?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Why North Korea's Kim Jong Un doesn't need a US deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7ec549c549b3ed62527323bc71edffb1e8f0637881a8c8423e14fc370835c678</id><updated>2026-09-12T04:45:10Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T10:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-north-korea-s-kim-jong-un-doesn-t-need-a-us-deal/a-79227854--e7f102464964.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-north-korea-s-kim-jong-un-doesn-t-need-a-us-deal/a-79227854?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump's overtures to North Korea's dictator have gone nowhere, with an emboldened Pyongyang accelerating its nuclear program and solidifying alliances with Russia and China.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen: Houthis tighten control of strategic Red Sea towns</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:35b4e3a035fe9fe5e3bdd26c1dc634657317fd5d34cc222282b9870a924f5d59</id><updated>2026-09-12T04:45:10Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T10:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/yemen-houthis-tighten-control-of-strategic-red-sea-towns/a-79220628--4b086e3863b4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/yemen-houthis-tighten-control-of-strategic-red-sea-towns/a-79220628?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Reports indicate Houthi militants have taken over the port city of Mokha along with Perim Island, which occupies a strategic position on a vital transport waterway in the Red Sea.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Turks in Germany anxious after AfD wins in Saxony-Anhalt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bda56ccb9b8cf8805648b59b2187ac525c35a62c51a368b1be4a7dd0289442af</id><updated>2026-09-12T04:45:10Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T10:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turks-in-germany-anxious-after-afd-wins-in-saxony-anhalt/a-79221764--9bdd69d84853.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turks-in-germany-anxious-after-afd-wins-in-saxony-anhalt/a-79221764?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Alternative for Germany party's win in Saxony-Anhalt has alarmed people of Turkish origin in eastern states. Will workers and business owners abandon the increasingly AfD-friendly region for the more welcoming west?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>China angered by Taiwan VP's visit to EU democracy forum</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:02d942d1dc9f0a3a70b85a245f744e25e5bce4a6169fe58ccf102d2c9ea62e2a</id><updated>2026-09-12T04:45:10Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T10:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-angered-by-taiwan-vp-s-visit-to-eu-democracy-forum/a-79226311--51b6e60ff469.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-angered-by-taiwan-vp-s-visit-to-eu-democracy-forum/a-79226311?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Beijing has lodged a complaint with Italy and the EU over top Taiwanese officials visiting a democracy conference. The EU is navigating contentious issues with China and high-ranking Taiwanese visits are rare.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>The 'end of an era' as Goethe-Institut in Russia closes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b7fc7376d063d3ee96757e83d4a41c679acd46e2be2368666e7f5dcffe493d5a</id><updated>2026-09-12T04:45:10Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T09:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-end-of-an-era-as-goethe-institut-in-russia-closes/a-79224321--189393464061.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-end-of-an-era-as-goethe-institut-in-russia-closes/a-79224321?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Goethe-Institut was one of the last German institutions still operating in Russia. However, following Moscow's decision to close its offices, all employees will have to stop working by September 13.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Far right lead in upcoming state election polls</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:03a3951c9040a401bb1507701e0a1d4df5bcab4ab2948c575639b07184545293</id><updated>2026-09-12T04:45:10Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T09:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-far-right-lead-in-upcoming-state-election-polls/live-79223427--90302ab1c910.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-far-right-lead-in-upcoming-state-election-polls/live-79223427?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Polling suggests the far-right AfD is carrying its momentum into another upcoming state election. Meanwhile, former Chancellor Angela Merkel has urged people not to take democracy for granted. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Hong Kong Tiananmen activists jailed for up to 7 years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:23539a3efe7b3ecbe3ee2cbcdf7eed0b1c390a709ebdb8bd2dbf9bb31da946ca</id><updated>2026-09-12T04:45:10Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T08:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hong-kong-tiananmen-activists-jailed-for-up-to-7-years/a-79224243--b40cd2f6f0ea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hong-kong-tiananmen-activists-jailed-for-up-to-7-years/a-79224243?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Three pro-democracy activists who organized annual commemorations of China's deadly 1989 Tiananmen crackdown were charged under Hong Kong's Beijing-backed national security law.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Magyar vs. Moscow: Hungary toughens stance toward Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:beb1d109251bd7f04715c220d61985e131e8c2a925f1a5337b022f6808a3e348</id><updated>2026-09-12T04:45:10Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T08:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/magyar-vs-moscow-hungary-toughens-stance-toward-russia/a-79223424--a42f60a005da.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/magyar-vs-moscow-hungary-toughens-stance-toward-russia/a-79223424?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Peter Magyar has abruptly ended the era of his predecessor's warm relations with Russia: Hungary has expelled 10 Russian diplomats. The Kremlin is considering halting gas supplies in response.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Philippines ferry fire: Search continues for dozens missing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:06ec8fbff80029cb4171bc8f574a8510cf9b2cf9b781334c143ead0b08d06af5</id><updated>2026-09-12T04:45:10Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T08:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/philippines-ferry-fire-search-continues-for-dozens-missing/a-79223425--fc38c9af4128.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/philippines-ferry-fire-search-continues-for-dozens-missing/a-79223425?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Firefighters searching for survivors combed through the smoking remains of a ferry off the coast of Coron island in the Philippines. Dozens of people have died, and more than 40 have been rescued.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's connection to the 9/11 attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:906dced0787da2a940588a14eb9fcf77743e955b056e97359a763defb3bf4902</id><updated>2026-09-12T04:45:10Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T06:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-connection-to-the-9-11-attacks/a-79202918--33622f8e5007.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-connection-to-the-9-11-attacks/a-79202918?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The 9/11 plot, including the twin tower attacks, was partly planned by the so-called Hamburg cell. A look at how Germany's national security was reshaped.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
